---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '@/components/Prose.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import hero from '@/assets/training/prenatal-yoga.jpeg';

const registerUrl = 'https://SivanandaToronto.as.me/?appointmentType=18746538';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Prenatal Yoga Teacher Training"
  lead="Learn to adapt yoga safely for each stage of pregnancy — Yoga Alliance continuing education."
  description="Prenatal Yoga Teacher Training (online) at the Toronto Sivananda Yoga Vedanta Centre."
  heroImage={hero}
  heroAlt="Prenatal yoga teacher training"
  narrow
>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Adapted yoga poses can physically and mentally help prepare women for childbirth. This course
      teaches you how to adapt a yoga practice to each stage of pregnancy, to ensure a safe and
      enriching practice for mother and baby. It counts as a 15-hour Continuing Education
      Certificate with Yoga Alliance.
    </p>
    <p>
      You will learn about the benefits of yoga in pregnancy and how to modify asanas for the
      changing body. We introduce special poses, breathing exercises and relaxation techniques to
      help prepare women for a smooth delivery, and explore how meditation and relaxation practices
      can help parents welcome their new children. The emphasis is on building a safe and supportive
      environment in the classroom and supporting students emotionally through their pregnancy
      journey.
    </p>

    <h2>In this course you will learn</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The benefits of yoga during pregnancy.</li>
      <li>How to adapt basic asanas.</li>
      <li>Special poses, breathing exercises and relaxation techniques.</li>
      <li>How to create a safe and supportive environment for your students.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Based on the teachings of the Sivananda Yoga Vedanta Organization, but open to yoga teachers
      of all traditions. Course dates are announced through the year — please check upcoming events
      or contact us.
    </p>

    <h2>Your teacher</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Sarada</strong> has been part of the Sivananda organization as a karma yogi and teacher
      for over 20 years, in South America, Canada and Europe. A kind and compassionate teacher, she offers
      her vast knowledge of yoga to a wide variety of students, and also teaches classes for kids and
      teens with special needs.
    </p>
  </Prose>

  <div class="mt-8"><Button href={registerUrl} external>Register</Button></div>
</PageLayout>
